Z||000000||Sootah||12-25-2001||02:20 AM||||OK, several of you are now probably aware of the apparent thing going on with me and West Coast Fiero. Now I just need to get my car from Cedar City, UT to Los Angeles, CA. Shipping almost any way I've looked into it is &gt;$500. Which doing it this way is still cheaper than going any other way, but I'd like to keep the cost as low as possible. If needed I can refer you to my previous rant.<P>Anyway, my main question would be: How do I get rates on backshipping? I know that there are a lot of trucks coming into Utah from Cali and are looking for backloads, so I need to figure out how I could go about getting prices on that. They'd have to give me a slightly better deal than the other options (you'd think) since its better to haul something than nothing (Duh).<P>I've checked into U-Haul and all that, but after mileage, gas, and trailer+truck renting the cost comes out to only slightly less than just having the vehicle shipped outright. Any other ideas?<P>Thanx guys. <B><I>-Sootah</B></I><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__tig_sig2.gif">           <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>The Black Beauty</A> (85 GT) - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Bustedato</A> (86 SE, Parts car)<BR><I>Don't sweat the petty things, and don't pet the sweaty things</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AOL IM</B>: KSSouter<BR><B>MSN IM</B>: I_R_Sootah@hotmail.com<BR></sup>||||reg||1
